          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "चटाना — caṭānā — \"to give (a baby) something to lick\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "माँ ने बच्चे को थोड़ा शहद चटाया। māṁ ne bacce ko thoṛā śahad caṭāyā. Mother gave the baby a little honey to lick."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past, with ने (he or she …): उसने बच्चे को दवा चटाई, usne bacce ko davā caṭāī."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "चटाना (caṭānā) is the causative partner of cāṭnā, \"to lick\", which CDIAL lists under caṭṭ, a form it reconstructs (CDIAL 4573). Medicine for small children is often given this way, mixed with honey."
            }
          ]
        },
