              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "काढ़ा (kāṛhā) is probably the noun of kāṛhnā, \"to pull out\", which CDIAL lists under kaḍḍhati, a form it reconstructs (CDIAL 2660): what boiling draws out of herbs. The link of senses is not given by CDIAL."
            }
          ]
